    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1362">

                <pb facs="1616" n="1418" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/7–2845</note>
                <head>No. 1362<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The British
                            Embassy to the Department of
                    State</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Aide-Mémoire</hi></p>
                <p>His Majesty’s Ambassador at Paris<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1362-f1"/> has been
                    instructed to inform the French Government that His Majesty’s Government are now
                    able to agree to the participation of the Soviet Government at the Paris talks
                    about Tangier and to suggest that the French and British Ambassadors in
                        Moscow<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1362-f2"/> should be instructed to make a joint
                    formal <pb facs="1617" n="1419" xml:id="pg1419"/> communication to the Soviet
                    Government, in reply to their representations in Paris and London of July
                        2nd,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1362-f3"/> inviting them to attend talks in Paris
                    early in August.</p>
                <p>Mr. Duff Cooper is further to inform the
                    French Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="4" xml:id="d1362-f4"/> that, in
                    line with the previous assurance of His Majesty’s Government, the general
                    question of Tangier has not been discussed at Potsdam and that no reference will
                    be made to Tangier in the communiqué to be issued at the end of the
                    Conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        G. H. M[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >iddleton</hi>]
                    </signed>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-28">July 28th,
                            1945</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
